    {
      "_id": "c2e9637dd5664670",
      "name": "Obfuscate — 3 Advanced — Phantom Haunter",
      "type": "power",
      "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>Reaches into a target's self-image and lets the Malkavian assume the appearance and false memories of whoever has most shaped (or damaged) that self-image &mdash; a sire, a parent, a priest, or whoever the target's own psyche supplies.</p><p><strong>MET System:</strong> Win a Social Challenge against the victim. On a win, you gain a free retest on your very next use of Dementation, Dominate, or Presence against that same victim. Once the retest is used, the power's knowledge fades unless you spend a Willpower Trait to keep it active for one further retest (this is expensive, but more certain than triggering the power again from scratch). You may only claim one retest per challenge this way. This power relies heavily on the target's own good-faith roleplaying &mdash; if the subject's player won't cooperate, don't force it with a Storyteller ruling.</p>",
        "source": "Clanbook: Malkavian, Chapter Two",
